<title>FRANCE: Rorer puts Centeon charge at $0.44/shr.</title>
<headline>Rorer puts Centeon charge at $0.44/shr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer said in a statement that the 1996 costs of the albumin products recall of its Centeon joint venture with Hoechst was $0.44 per share.</p>
<p>Centeon LCC said on January 24 it had resumed production after an October 10 recall of its in-date lots of albumin products as a precaution against risks of bacterial infection.</p>
<p>Centeon said it had made a number of modifications to its production and control processes.</p>
</text>
